### 引理 1

当 $t\downarrow0$ 时，

<a id="eq-5"></a>

$$
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\mathscr K'(t)&=\frac12\log t+O(1),\\
\mathscr K''(t)&=\frac1{2t}+O(1),\\
\mathscr K(t)
&=
S+\frac12t\log t
+\frac{\gamma-1+\log(2\pi)}2\,t
+O(t^2|\log t|).
\end{aligned}
}
\tag{5}
$$

因此存在一个固定的

$$
0<\delta<\log2
$$

使得

<a id="eq-6"></a>

$$
\boxed{
\mathscr K(t)>0,\qquad
\mathscr K'(t)<0,\qquad
\mathscr K''(t)>0
\quad(0<t\le\delta).
}
\tag{6}
$$

